nodes.body:
Agreed — added four tests to the existing `tests/v1/cudagraph/test_breakable_cudagraph.py` suite (`848c466a7`):

- unresolvable layer name and a drifted signature (non-str `layer_name`) both **raise at capture** with the sparse-only message — the two ways the gate can fail closed today;
- a stubbed `impl.is_sparse=True` layer is **captured inline** (fn runs, `add_eager` untouched);
- flag **off** keeps the eager-break path (exactly one `add_eager` call), so the gate cannot leak into the default behavior.

All 30 tests in the file pass on the validation env (GLM-5.3-Flash boot + mixed-batch probes on SM120, 8x 6000D). The refusal tests are the regression net you asked for: any future change that lets dense MLA back through the sparse check turns them red.

